# QGIS project

`{{ p.id }}.qgz` is the project that produced the delivered figures. Built and exported with QGIS {{ qgis_version }}.

1. Install the fonts in `../fonts/inter`.
2. Open `{{ p.id }}.qgz` in QGIS 3.34 or later. Keep the package folder whole; the project uses relative paths.
3. Project > Layouts lists one print layout per figure{% if atlases %} and one atlas layout per map book{% endif %}. View > Map themes switches the main window between figures.

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `{{ p.id }}.qgz` | Project: layers, symbols, labels, map themes, print layouts |
| `build_qgis_project.py` | Rebuilds the project and all exports from `../spec/map_package.json`. Needs only QGIS |
| `Rebuild_Maps_Processing.py` | The same rebuild as a QGIS Processing tool (Processing > Toolbox > Scripts > Add Script to Toolbox) |
| `styles/*.qml` | One style file per layer per figure |
| `layouts/*.qpt` | Layout templates |
| `qgis_build_report.json` | What the build produced |
| `AGENT_PROMPT.md` | Checks and rebuild steps for a person or AI agent |
